              "sequence": 1,
              "lessonLabel": "Lesson 1",
              "linkLabel": "Lit./Mythology",
              "title": "30m Lit./Mythology: Grades 7-8 - Lesson 1",
              "body": "Gertrudis Gómez de Avellaneda\n⍞ Materials: Lightning Dreamer\n\n➜ INTRO\nToday we will begin a novel in verse about the Cuban-Spanish Romantic poet Gertrudis Gómez de Avellaneda (1814-1873) who used her writing to speak out against injustice of all kinds. If you have not read her biography already, it is linked below.\n∞ Article Link: Biography of Gertrudis Gomez de Avellaneda\n\n➜ READ, NARRATE & DISCUSS\n1. p.169-174 \"Historical Note\"\n2. p.ix \"Historical Background\"\n3. p.3-10 \"Books are door-shaped\" - \"like oxen or mules.\"\n\n• Who are the people? Make a character list. Each week as you read, think about the different perspectives of the poems and how each one sees the same situation very differently. Share your observations in your narrations.\n\n• How do the alternating viewpoints allow the poems to speak to each other? Look for poems that discuss the same topic but from different perspectives.",
              "teacherNotes": "• EXTRA HELPING\n∞ Link: What Are Free Verse Poems",
              "editUrl": "https://airtable.com/apphTWdjAdJEcAmoe/pago27hsdn3q8TtGK?XRKkD=recrSWSoC0yNwPHrT&6J82c=recY7gajs76FmeY9C",
              "lessonLinksUrl": "https://planning.alveary.org/links.html?id=recrSWSoC0yNwPHrT&term=1&week=1",
              "links": [
                {
                  "text": "What Are Free Verse Poems",
                  "url": "https://youtu.be/13cW2vXOMxU?si=2eiDG96US6j9Sy8d"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "lessonId": "recI2Sjg3uHub9lHL",
              "termNumber": 1,
              "termLabel": "Term 1",
              "weekNumber": 2,
              "weekLabel": "Week 2",
              "sequence": 2,
              "lessonLabel": "Lesson 2",
              "linkLabel": "Lit./Mythology",
              "title": "30m Lit./Mythology: Grades 7-8 - Lesson 2",
              "body": "Lightning Dreamer, cont.\n⍞ Materials: Lightning Dreamer\n\n➜ RECAP\nWhat were your first impressions of these poems? \n\n➜ READ, NARRATE & DISCUSS\np.11-24 \"I feel like a new person\" - \"dark or light.\"\n\n• How are the nuns able to support Tula?\n• How did Tula's father influence her, and how has his death shaped who she is at thirteen?\n• Why does Tula feel she is not so different from the slave girls she views from the barred window? \n• Continue to add to your character list.",
              "teacherNotes": "• COMPOSITION\nWhat role do books and reading have on the story so far? How are the \"rules\" different for Tula? Caridad? The nuns?\n\n• EXTRA HELPING\n∞ Link: José María Heredia biography",
              "editUrl": "https://airtable.com/apphTWdjAdJEcAmoe/pago27hsdn3q8TtGK?XRKkD=recrSWSoC0yNwPHrT&6J82c=recI2Sjg3uHub9lHL",
              "lessonLinksUrl": "https://planning.alveary.org/links.html?id=recrSWSoC0yNwPHrT&term=1&week=2",
              "links": [
                {
                  "text": "José María Heredia biography",
                  "url": "https://poets.org/poet/jose-maria-heredia"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "lessonId": "recwYuXxLjpsBzQqd",
              "termNumber": 1,
              "termLabel": "Term 1",
              "weekNumber": 3,
              "weekLabel": "Week 3",
              "sequence": 3,
              "lessonLabel": "Lesson 3",
              "linkLabel": "Lit./Mythology",
              "title": "30m Lit./Mythology: Grades 7-8 - Lesson 3",
              "body": "⍞ Materials: Lightning Dreamer\n\n➜ RECAP   \nHow would you describe this book (so far) to someone who had never read it?\n\n➜ READ, NARRATE, & DISCUSS\np.25-35\n\n• How do the decisions Tula's mother made differ from what she expects from Tula? What is your impression of her mother so far?\n• Why does Tula feels she can free herself \"only with words\"? \n• Why is Tula not allowed to read books? What are her mother and stepfather afraid of happening if she reads books?",
              "teacherNotes": "",
              "editUrl": "https://airtable.com/apphTWdjAdJEcAmoe/pago27hsdn3q8TtGK?XRKkD=recrSWSoC0yNwPHrT&6J82c=recwYuXxLjpsBzQqd",
              "lessonLinksUrl": "",
              "links": []
            },
            {
              "lessonId": "recuIZXvEa9qOMomV",
              "termNumber": 1,
              "termLabel": "Term 1",
              "weekNumber": 4,
              "weekLabel": "Week 4",
              "sequence": 4,
              "lessonLabel": "Lesson 4",
              "linkLabel": "Lit./Mythology",
              "title": "30m Lit./Mythology: Grades 7-8 - Lesson 4",
              "body": "⍞ Materials: Lightning Dreamer\n\n➜ RECAP \nWhat did we learn about Tula's situation in the last chapter? What does her future hold? \n\n➜ READ, NARRATE, & DISCUSS\np.39-55\n\n• What have we learned about Caridad and why she might not want to share stories of her childhood?\n• What need does the orphan theater fill for Tula? Why does she have to change the stories her plays tell?",
              "teacherNotes": "",
              "editUrl": "https://airtable.com/apphTWdjAdJEcAmoe/pago27hsdn3q8TtGK?XRKkD=recrSWSoC0yNwPHrT&6J82c=recuIZXvEa9qOMomV",
              "lessonLinksUrl": "",
              "links": []
