            {
              "lessonId": "rec5J07dedEiBrkT1",
              "termNumber": 1,
              "termLabel": "Term 1",
              "weekNumber": 6,
              "weekLabel": "Week 6",
              "sequence": 6,
              "lessonLabel": "Lesson 6",
              "linkLabel": "Lit./Mythology",
              "title": "30m Lit./Mythology: Grades 7-8 - Lesson 6",
              "body": "⍞ Materials: Lightning Dreamer\n\n➜ RECAP \nWhat injustice does Tula experience in the last reading? \n\n➜ READ, NARRATE, & DISCUSS\np.73-90 \n\n• Has your impression of Tula's mother changed at all throughout the story? \n• Do Manuel's actions change your perception of him? How has he supported Tula throughout the story?",
              "teacherNotes": "• COMPOSITION\nCompare the concerns of Tula, Manuel, Caridad, Mama, and the Nuns in pages 73-83. Are they justified or not given the time and setting? \n\n★ TEACHER NOTE\nThe tertulias brought people together in quiet defiance. They were often political rebellion disguised as parties; a way of sharing counterculture ideas in places where fascist regimes had made it dangerous, even illegal, to gather.",
              "editUrl": "https://airtable.com/apphTWdjAdJEcAmoe/pago27hsdn3q8TtGK?XRKkD=recrSWSoC0yNwPHrT&6J82c=rec5J07dedEiBrkT1",
              "lessonLinksUrl": "",
              "links": []
            },
            {
              "lessonId": "recS3nXrlT8whXXau",
              "termNumber": 1,
              "termLabel": "Term 1",
              "weekNumber": 7,
              "weekLabel": "Week 7",
              "sequence": 7,
              "lessonLabel": "Lesson 7",
              "linkLabel": "Lit./Mythology",
              "title": "30m Lit./Mythology: Grades 7-8 - Lesson 7",
              "body": "⍞ Materials: Lightning Dreamer\n\n➜ RECAP\nWhat risks were Tula and Manuel taking in the last reading? \n\n➜ READ, NARRATE, & DISCUSS\np.90-109\n\n• How does Tula learn to hide her messages? \n• What are some of the acts of defiance and courage in the book so far and what are their consequences? \n• Why does Mama imagine their lives will be peaceful and prosperous once Tula is married? Do you think she's right?",
              "teacherNotes": "",
              "editUrl": "https://airtable.com/apphTWdjAdJEcAmoe/pago27hsdn3q8TtGK?XRKkD=recrSWSoC0yNwPHrT&6J82c=recS3nXrlT8whXXau",
              "lessonLinksUrl": "",
              "links": []
            },
            {
              "lessonId": "recMJCcS5LJLhYs00",
              "termNumber": 1,
              "termLabel": "Term 1",
              "weekNumber": 8,
              "weekLabel": "Week 8",
              "sequence": 8,
              "lessonLabel": "Lesson 8",
              "linkLabel": "Lit./Mythology",
              "title": "30m Lit./Mythology: Grades 7-8 - Lesson 8",
              "body": "⍞ Materials: Lightning Dreamer\n\n➜ RECAP \nWhat do you think will happen next?  \n\n➜ READ, NARRATE, & DISCUSS \np.113-127\n\n• Why can't Tula write even though she now has a degree of freedom with her Uncle gone? \n• Why does Tula leave the plantation even though she's now left alone there?",
              "teacherNotes": "",
              "editUrl": "https://airtable.com/apphTWdjAdJEcAmoe/pago27hsdn3q8TtGK?XRKkD=recrSWSoC0yNwPHrT&6J82c=recMJCcS5LJLhYs00",
              "lessonLinksUrl": "",
              "links": []
            },
            {
              "lessonId": "recVpCrIAcwqoC61V",
              "termNumber": 1,
              "termLabel": "Term 1",
              "weekNumber": 9,
              "weekLabel": "Week 9",
              "sequence": 9,
              "lessonLabel": "Lesson 9",
              "linkLabel": "Lit./Mythology",
              "title": "30m Lit./Mythology: Grades 7-8 - Lesson 9",
              "body": "⍞ Materials: Lightning Dreamer\n\n➜ RECAP \nWhat was plantation life like for Tula with her Uncle gone? \n\n➜ READ, NARRATE, & DISCUSS\np.128-144\n\n• What happens when some of Tula's fantasies about love meet reality? \n• What things do Sab and Tula have in common despite their differences? What insights does Sab's godmother give them?",
              "teacherNotes": "• COMPOSITION\nExplore how Sab and Tula are reflections of each other's freedom dreams. How are their dreams alike? Different?",
              "editUrl": "https://airtable.com/apphTWdjAdJEcAmoe/pago27hsdn3q8TtGK?XRKkD=recrSWSoC0yNwPHrT&6J82c=recVpCrIAcwqoC61V",
              "lessonLinksUrl": "",
              "links": []
